        -:   99:/**
        -:  100: * Abstract dimension API
        -:  101: *
        -:  102: * Some notes about dimension nomenclature:
        -:  103: *
        -:  104: * - "feature points" are the points being measured by the dimension.  For an example, the start
        -:  105: *   and end points of a line to be measured.  These are the first points picked when drawing a
        -:  106: *   new dimension.  Dimensions can have one or more feature points: linear dimensions (the only
        -:  107: *   type supported in KiCad 5 and earlier) have two feature points; leader dimensions have one;
        -:  108: *   and ordinate dimensions can have in theory an unlimited number of feature points.
        -:  109: *
        -:  110: * - "feature lines" are lines that coincide with feature points.  Not all dimension types have
        -:  111: *   feature lines.  The actual start and end of feature lines is calculated from dimension style
        -:  112: *   properties (offset from feature point to start of feature line, height of crossbar, and height
        -:  113: *   of feature line past crossbar, for example in linear dimensions)
        -:  114: *
        -:  115: * - "crossbar" refers to the perpendicular line (usually with arrows at each end) between feature
        -:  116: *   lines on linear dimensions
        -:  117: */
